  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">INTEGRATED CONSERVATION ACTIVITIES IN TH</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will: 1) Restore (1,319 hectares/3,257.93 acres) of seasonal wetlands as migratory waterfowl and shorebird habitat in a previously protected area by (a) reducing sedimentation and eutrophication through soil conservation techniques in the middle watershed, (b) cleaning and desilting seasonal streams and channels, and (c) building containers for solid waste disposal. 2) Enhance water quality on (103 hectares/254.41 acres) through the construction and rehabilitation of sewage systems and an artificial wetland for wastewater treatment and the installation of 100 dry toilets and 20 biodigesters. 3) Survey habitat use by waterfowl and shorebirds and monitor habitat productivity. 4) Train 200 teachers and educate 2,000 students in environmental topics, train 100 farmers in alternative farming and ranching techniques, and conduct outreach to surrounding local communities</narrative>
  </description>
